## Purpose

Turn the generic starter capabilities into a topic-specific dependency path without claiming a measured baseline. This module is the initial owner of all starter skill IDs; split ownership into later modules only after updating the tracker and validation markers together.

## Entry evidence

- No learner competence is assumed.
- Available capacity and constraints are recorded as known, unknown, or provisional.

## Work

1. Preserve an unaided model of {{TOPIC}}.
2. Attempt the baseline diagnostic.
3. Define the smallest defensible capstone or readiness condition.
4. Rewrite S01–S08 as topic-specific observable capabilities while preserving their IDs.
5. Record prerequisites, source authority, practice modes, and safety boundaries.

## Exit gate

The skill tracker, roadmap, first week, practice route, and capstone criteria agree; all learner statuses remain `Not started` unless real evidence was produced after scaffolding.
